---
import PlaygroundShell from '../../components/PlaygroundShell.astro';
import RangeField from '../../components/RangeField.astro';
---
<PlaygroundShell title="Back-of-the-envelope numbers" hint="How many cache fills a huge cache does each day, what it would cost to log every one of them, and what 'N nines of consistency' means in wrong writes. A teaching model with round numbers, not Meta's system or data.">
  <div class="pg est" data-est>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <RangeField label="Queries per day (trillions)" name="q" min="100" max="2000" step="100" value="1000" />
      <RangeField label="Cache hit rate (%)" name="h" min="90" max="99.9" step="0.1" value="99" />
      <RangeField label="Bytes per log line" name="l" min="50" max="1000" step="50" value="200" />
      <RangeField label="Share of fills that fall in a write's race window (%)" name="w" min="0.001" max="1" step="0.001" value="0.01" />
      <RangeField label="Writes per day (billions)" name="x" min="10" max="1000" step="10" value="100" />
      <RangeField label="Nines of consistency (within 5 minutes)" name="n" min="6" max="10" value="10" />
    </div>
    <dl class="est-out" data-out aria-live="polite"></dl>
    <p class="pg-note">Teaching model, not Meta's system or data. From Meta's 2022 post: TAO serves more than one quadrillion queries a day (1,000 trillion), which at a 99 percent hit rate means more than 10 trillion cache fills a day. The same post says consistency of TAO rose, by one measure, from 99.9999 percent (6 nines) to 99.99999999 percent (10 nines) at the five-minute timescale, meaning fewer than 1 in 10 billion cache writes inconsistent after five minutes. Guesses of mine that you can change: 200 bytes per log line, 0.01 percent of fills inside a race window, and 100 billion writes per day. Assumptions: every query that misses the cache causes one fill, a day has 86,400 seconds, and the rate of wrong writes is exactly the one the nines give. The real figures were not published for these inputs.</p>
  </div>
</PlaygroundShell>
<script>
  import { query, numberValue } from '../../playground';
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-est]').forEach((root) => {
    const q = query(root);
    const val = numberValue(q);
    const OUT_ROWS = 10; // lines in the result list
    const SECONDS_PER_DAY = 86400, TRILLION = 1e12, BILLION = 1e9, GB = 1e9, TB = 1e12, BASE_NINES = 6;
    const rows = Array.from({ length: OUT_ROWS }, () => { const dt = document.createElement('dt'); const dd = document.createElement('dd'); q('[data-out]').append(dt, dd); return { dt, dd }; });
    const fmt = (n: number) => (n >= 100 ? Math.round(n) : Number(n.toPrecision(3))).toLocaleString('en-US', { maximumFractionDigits: 6 });
    function draw() {
      ['q', 'h', 'l', 'w', 'x', 'n'].forEach((key) => (q(`[data-${key}val]`).textContent = String(val(`[data-${key}]`))));
      const queries = val('[data-q]') * TRILLION; const miss = 1 - val('[data-h]') / 100; const bytes = val('[data-l]');
      const windowShare = val('[data-w]') / 100; const writes = val('[data-x]') * BILLION; const nines = val('[data-n]');
      const fills = queries * miss;
      const wrong = writes * Math.pow(10, -nines);
      const data: [string, string][] = [
        ['Cache fills per day (trillions)', fmt(fills / TRILLION)],
        ['Cache fills per second (billions)', fmt(fills / SECONDS_PER_DAY / BILLION)],
        ['Log data per day if every fill is traced (TB)', fmt((fills * bytes) / TB)],
        ['Log data per day if only fills in a race window are traced (GB)', fmt((fills * windowShare * bytes) / GB)],
        ['Log lines per day if only the race window is traced (billions)', fmt((fills * windowShare) / BILLION)],
        ['Logging saved by tracing only the window', `${fmt(1 / windowShare)} times less`],
        [`With ${nines} nines, one wrong write in every (billions of writes)`, fmt(Math.pow(10, nines) / BILLION)],
        ['Wrong writes per day at that rate', fmt(wrong)],
        [`Wrong writes compared with ${BASE_NINES} nines`, nines === BASE_NINES ? 'the same' : `${fmt(Math.pow(10, nines - BASE_NINES))} times fewer`],
        ['Days between wrong writes, on average', wrong > 0 ? fmt(1 / wrong) : 'never'],
      ];
      rows.forEach((r, i) => { r.dt.textContent = data[i][0]; r.dd.textContent = data[i][1]; });
    }
    root.addEventListener('input', draw);
    draw();
  });
</script>
